// Chief Marlow — the "Clear the Deck" bounty (quest 2): get Vex off the plaza,
// report back, get paid. The payment is the quest's reward now, not a give_item
// here (quest-system.md Phase 4) — there are two ways to finish this and only
// one of them used to run through this conversation's turn-in line.
//
// The two routes are read here the same way the quest's stage condition and
// Vex's own conversation read them — npc_defeated, or the flag his payoff sets
// — rather than through the stage they both reach: a turn-in should depend on
// the world, not on a summary of it. Marlow has an opinion about which.

title: entry
---
<<if quest_state(2, "Success")>>
    <<jump already_done>>
<<elseif quest_state(2, "InProgress")>>
    <<jump inprogress>>
<<else>>
    <<jump offer>>
<<endif>>
===

title: inprogress
---
<<if npc_defeated("intro.vex")>>
    <<jump beaten_turnin>>
<<elseif flag("vex_paid")>>
    <<jump bought_turnin>>
<<else>>
    <<jump inprogress_waiting>>
<<endif>>
===

title: offer
---
<<if npc_defeated("intro.vex")>>
    <<jump offer_downed>>
<<elseif flag("vex_paid")>>
    <<jump offer_bought>>
<<else>>
    <<jump offer_pending>>
<<endif>>
===

title: already_done
---
$npc: Deck's been quiet since you dealt with Vex. Keep that keycard handy — it opens more doors than you'd think.
===

title: inprogress_waiting
---
$npc: Vex is still strutting around the plaza like he owns it. The keycard's yours the moment that changes.
===

title: offer_pending
---
$npc: See that red-suited thug by the plaza? Vex. He's been shaking down every courier on this deck and my hands are tied. Get him off my plaza and there's a maintenance keycard in it for you.
-> I'll handle Vex
    <<set_quest 2 InProgress>>
    $npc: I don't much mind how. Watch yourself either way — he doesn't fight fair, and he keeps a drone at his back.
-> Not my problem
    <<jump declined>>
===

title: offer_downed
---
$npc: Word is somebody already put Vex on the deck plates. That was you, wasn't it? I was about to post a bounty on him — say the word and it's yours.
-> That was me
    <<set_quest 2 InProgress>>
    <<jump beaten_turnin>>
-> Not my problem
    <<jump declined>>
===

title: offer_bought
---
$npc: Word is Vex packed up and took his business two decks down, and that credits changed hands over it. Yours?
-> Mine
    <<set_quest 2 InProgress>>
    <<jump bought_turnin>>
-> Not my problem
    <<jump declined>>
===

title: declined
---
$npc: Then keep your credits out of his reach, and don't say I didn't warn you.
===

// The keycard itself comes from the quest's reward, so it arrives on either
// route without this conversation handing it over.
title: beaten_turnin
---
<<play_anim Use_Item>>
<<set_quest 2 Success>>
$npc: So the deck finally goes quiet. A deal's a deal — here's the maintenance keycard. It'll open doors most people never get to see.
===

title: bought_turnin
---
<<play_anim Use_Item>>
<<set_quest 2 Success>>
$npc: Bought him off. Not how I'd have done it, and he'll be somebody else's problem by morning — but the plaza's quiet and a deal's a deal. Keycard's yours.
===
